@prefix fw: <http://example.org/backlog-framework-register#> .

#################################################################
#  v1.1.0 (2026-09-07, brsf-session) -- FIVE BYPASSES, MEASURED. All
#  five toy lineages first appear in git at dcb5f9b with their items
#  and no Stage_Backlog output. Findings exactly as the tool emitted
#  them; each lineage frozen by its finding until a restart answers it
#  in a later commit. Also in this commit, the transformations that
#  must PRECEDE a transform-and-conquer restart (the git witness will
#  refuse a restart that comes before them):
#    TS: a ScopeChange narrowing TS_Scope to TS_D1 (instance
#        simplification -- TS_D2 was never served by any item);
#    TR: nothing to add -- TR_EP already decomposes into TR_S_PL, as
#        every epic in this framework must (EpicDecomposedShape, L4).
#        Recorded as a finding: in a conformant register the
#        representation change is always already done; see G85.
#    TT: the template is fw:L_ChangeDiscipline, a real lineage of the
#        main register that reads ORDERED; named on the restart.
#################################################################
